# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# seed/host/hostpool/hostpool.cases: run-time pools as host-word byte operands (fzcore round 3, lead item 5), run by
# the OM-2 conductor (seed/qualification/om2/gate.om) from seed/host/check.sh.
# fixture: hostpool.om checks 1-6 (see its notes): argread, stat and fopen on pools, a pool that moves while the
# operands are read, the trap past its length, a 4.8 MB argument vector built in pools reaching a new image under a
# 64 MiB stack limit, and the kernel E2BIG for the same vector under 8 MiB.
# oracle: execfds /usr/bin/env with a 70-entry environment built in a pool; env70.want is the output of oracle.py,
# compared again by seed/host/check.sh.
# Refusals that stay: target x86linux has no pools (25); the device, mapping, VFIO and KFD words keep error 7
# (devctl.om, kfdctl.om); a pool is still never a function argument (fnarg.om, 19).
# Mutants: admit (harray refuses every pool again, as before this change): the fixture is error 7; devadmit
# (hpoolok admits every word): devctl.om compiles and runs into the request-size check of devctl (trap 3, exit 103),
# and kfdctl.om compiles and runs (its ioctl on descriptor -1 fails, exit 0); kfdadmit (hpoolok without only the
# KFD range 241..243): kfdctl.om compiles and runs while devctl.om is still error 7.
# legacy.om checks all six legacy pool operands through real exec/link/rename/symlink behavior, exact-limit
# controls and limit+1 traps, then one-byte-past-current-length traps (both execenv operands).
# execpure requires the same Linux Landlock/seccomp support as SECURITY-673; lack of it is failure, not a pass.
# Size mutants raise only the old hpack byte limits by one: legacy.om must fail check 9 (exec) or 11 (symlink).
deadline 120
fixture run seed/host/hostpool/hostpool.om - file:seed/host/hostpool/big.want - 0
oracle run seed/host/hostpool/hostpool.om - file:seed/host/hostpool/env70.want - 0 oracle
legacy run seed/host/hostpool/legacy.om - file:seed/host/hostpool/legacy.want - 0
x86 refuse seed/host/hostpool/x86-target.om+seed/host/hostpool/hostpool.om 25
devctl refuse seed/host/hostpool/devctl.om 7
kfdctl refuse seed/host/hostpool/kfdctl.om 7
fnarg refuse seed/host/hostpool/fnarg.om 19
subst seed/host/hostpool/mutants/admit.from seed/host/hostpool/mutants/admit.to
cc seed/omc/omc.om
mut-admit refuse seed/host/hostpool/hostpool.om 7
mut-legacy-admit refuse seed/host/hostpool/legacy.om 7
cc pinned
subst seed/host/hostpool/mutants/devadmit.from seed/host/hostpool/mutants/devadmit.to
cc seed/omc/omc.om
mut-devadmit run seed/host/hostpool/devctl.om - - - 103
mut-devadmit-kfd run seed/host/hostpool/kfdctl.om - - - 0
cc pinned
subst seed/host/hostpool/mutants/kfdadmit.from seed/host/hostpool/mutants/kfdadmit.to
cc seed/omc/omc.om
mut-kfdadmit run seed/host/hostpool/kfdctl.om - - - 0
mut-kfdadmit-dev refuse seed/host/hostpool/devctl.om 7
cc pinned
subst seed/host/hostpool/mutants/execsize.from seed/host/hostpool/mutants/execsize.to
cc seed/omc/omc.om
mut-execsize run seed/host/hostpool/legacy.om - - - 9
cc pinned
subst seed/host/hostpool/mutants/pathsize.from seed/host/hostpool/mutants/pathsize.to
cc seed/omc/omc.om
mut-pathsize run seed/host/hostpool/legacy.om - - - 11
cc pinned
